&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Every Identity, from AI to Human&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Identity is the key to unlocking the potential of AI. Okta secures AI by building the trusted, neutral infrastructure that enables organizations to safely embrace this new era. This work requires a relentless drive to solve complex challenges with real-world stakes. We are looking for builders and owners who operate with speed and urgency and execute with excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an opportunity to do career-defining work. We&#39;re all in on this mission. If you are too, let&#39;s talk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is to free everyone to safely use any technology. We promise to make identity work for everyone—whether you’re a developer looking to innovate or a security professional looking to mitigate. We are looking for curious, excited, boundary-pushing team members. So, if you’re a big thinker who is nimble and adaptable, Okta may be an ideal place to shine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Okta’s Customer Identity Cloud (CIC), powered by Auth0 technology, is an easy-to-implement authentication and authorization platform designed by developers for developers. We make access to applications safe, secure, and seamless for more than 100 million daily logins around the world. Our modern approach to identity enables this Tier 0 global service to deliver convenience, privacy, and security so customers can focus on innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a collaborative, developer-focused &lt;strong&gt;SDE2 iOS Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;Universal Components&lt;/strong&gt; team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You UNDERSTAND developers!&lt;/strong&gt; You know what they need, how to talk to them, how to make their lives easier, and what turns friction into delight. You recognize when a framework, library, or product provides an exceptional developer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an iOS Engineer on the Universal Components team, you will leverage that developer-first mindset to build and maintain our open-source UI components and SDKs. You will contribute to refining our entire developer journey—from onboarding, quickstarts, and documentation to providing direct assistance in developer channels. Your contributions will directly reach thousands of customer applications and carry a high impact across the mobile ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will act as an internal and external advocate for the iOS platforms and technologies you work with daily. Collaborating in a cross-functional environment alongside developer relations, onboarding, growth, dashboard, and core SDK teams, you will help deliver a world-class experience for our component libraries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The most vital qualifications for this position are solid software engineering fundamentals, strong empathy for developers, and a collaborative mindset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Building Modular UI:&lt;/strong&gt; Designing and developing composable, high-quality UI components from the ground up using SwiftUI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SDK Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Shaping and evolving our open-source Universal Components iOS SDK, ensuring seamless integration with core identity and authentication services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Authoring Developer Resources:&lt;/strong&gt; Writing, curating, and polishing technical content, including tutorials, guides, sample applications, and clear documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community &amp;amp; Advocacy:&lt;/strong&gt; Engaging directly with the open-source developer community, championing modern developer experience, and providing technical support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code Quality &amp;amp; Domain Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Serving as a key technical contributor by providing domain knowledge, participating in code reviews, and upholding quality standards across our iOS projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge Sharing:&lt;/strong&gt; Representing the team&#39;s technical expertise at developer events, community forums, or through technical blog posts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintenance &amp;amp; Modernization:&lt;/strong&gt; Troubleshooting, fixing, and maintaining client libraries while staying up to date with modern Apple frameworks and platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring to the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3 to 5 years&lt;/strong&gt; of professional experience in native iOS development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2+ years&lt;/strong&gt; of hands-on experience building production interfaces in &lt;strong&gt;SwiftUI&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to seamlessly translate design mocks (e.g., Figma) into clean, modular, and accessible SwiftUI code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong interest in developing reusable iOS libraries and SDKs consumed by third-party developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of modern iOS frameworks, Swift best practices, and the broader Apple ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or contributing to at least one shipped iOS application or public SDK using SwiftUI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical understanding of modern dependency managers and SDK distribution methods (e.g., Swift Package Manager, Carthage).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CI/CD platforms (e.g., GitHub Actions, CircleCI) and running automated mobile tests in continuous integration pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills with a proven track record of authoring developer documentation or technical content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative approach to engineering, with the ability to self-direct and execute independently while thriving in a globally distributed team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points If You Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge or hands-on experience with Design Systems&lt;/strong&gt; (building component libraries, design tokens, or multi-platform visual consistency).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with &lt;strong&gt;UIKit&lt;/strong&gt; and handling hybrid SwiftUI/UIKit architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in remote or distributed team environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;Android&lt;/strong&gt; (Kotlin &amp;amp; Jetpack Compose) or cross-platform architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active contributions to open-source projects or experience maintaining open-source repositories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A personal technical blog, open-source portfolio, or published articles on modern iOS development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic familiarity with identity, authentication protocols, or access management space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI - Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#Pid - P18991&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Okta Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://rewards.okta.com&quot;&gt;Supporting Your Well-Being&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/okta-for-good/&quot;&gt;Driving Social Impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/talent-connection-community/&quot;&gt;Developing Talent and Fostering Connection + Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
